expected_excess_after_ca_tax:
**The pick (buy and hold):** 0 pp/yr by definition. VOO or IVV beat SPY by only +0.03 to +0.04 pp/yr.

**Best alternative, the website 2x trend preset (SSO/IEF, SMA175, 3% band):**
* Central estimate about +1 pp/yr if the account is eventually sold. The plausible range for the true mean is -1 to +2.5.
* About 0 to +0.5 pp/yr if the shares are held until death (step-up) or given away.
* Actual 20-year results could land roughly 3 pp/yr either side of that, because tracking error is about 13.5%/yr. That is roughly a 1-in-3 to 1-in-2 chance of trailing SPY after tax over 20 years. If trends persist for only 1-3 months, it trails in 57-66% of resampled paths.

**Basis.** The starting point is the exact website config on real SSO, 2006-2026 in CA: full-period excess +3.67, p 0.116. Even in-sample that fails the p <= 0.10 item. I shrank it using:
* start-averaged excess to the end of +1.6 (2000-26) and +2.3 (1986-26);
* the 1930-85 holdout: full-period excess +1.5 to +2.5, p 0.16-0.29;
* the record since 2010: about 0 (2010s +0.6; 2020-26 -0.3 to -1.24; starts in 2010-23 average -0.47, 47% of them negative);
* 33 other equity markets, each against its own buy-and-hold: median +0.24, pooled -0.53 (p 0.60);
* the step-up, which costs -0.8 to -0.9;
* selection: SMA175/3% was the best of 34 neighbouring settings (+5.3 against a median of about +3.2), within-structure PBO is 0.5-0.8, and DSR is 0.002-0.006.

**Momentum preset:** about 0 (range -1 to +1).
